proposals.what:
Under `Your answer: left out the constant term` on a miss, four chips:
- `That's it` (default, no tap needed);
- `I slipped` (knew it; arithmetic or careless);
- `Misread` (answered a different question);
- `Rushed`.

Slip detection: when the learner's first-try accuracy on the type is 80% or more and the time was under half their median, `I slipped` is preselected, with the reason 'You usually get this type right, and this took 0:21.'

Filing:
- concept files the trap as today;
- slip and misread file R9 kind slip (owed 1, kept out of the misconception list and the crowd top-mistake stats);
- rushed files as slip, plus the pace note.

Summary:
- `Misses: 3 concept · 2 slips · 1 misread`.
- When slips come to 30% or more of misses, the line 'Slips cost as much as hard questions: 2 of your 3 Easy misses were slips.'
- An optional `Slip check` toggle for the next set: on Easy questions, Check needs a second tap on 'Checked the last step'.

SkillPanel: `slips 4 · concepts 6`.

At the top of the builder, above the presets, three large cards. Each is a fully specified set with its own Start pill:
- `Coach's pick · 10 q · ≈16 min · Percentages (2 mistakes), Circles (weakest)`;
- `Due today · 6 q · ≈8 min`;
- `Fix mistakes · 4 q · ≈6 min`.

A fourth, `Again: your last set`, appears once one exists. Enter on page load starts the first card, and a mono `Enter` hint shows on hover devices.

Each card has `Edit`, which loads it into the tree and settings below. Cards with nothing to serve show their reason in place of Start. Estimated minutes use the learner's own median pace.

parity_gaps.upgrade:
Make strikes data, which is possible because every struck option names a misconception:
- after answering, the verdict says 'You struck the key (C) before answering' when that happened;
- the summary shows strike accuracy;
- the SkillPanel shows `You reliably rule out: used the slope as the intercept (6 of 6)`.

Triage advice from the set's own data:
- 'Fill the 2 blanks with your best guess first: a blank scores the same as a wrong answer';
- then 'Revisit these 3 Unsure (2 min left, about 40 s each)';
- with each question's time shown in its cell.
